## Movement vs the last campaign (benchmarks/perf_gap_2026-08-11.meta, commit bdff3700f)

| preset | slope ratio 08-11 | slope ratio 08-13 | port slope 08-11 | port slope 08-13 | port/port |
|:------:|------------------:|------------------:|-----------------:|-----------------:|----------:|
| p2     | 4.12x             | **4.16x**         | 1929.67 ms/MP    | 1943.35 ms/MP    | 1.007     |
| p6     | 3.52x             | **3.39x**         |  133.73 ms/MP    |  131.13 ms/MP    | 0.981     |
| p10    | 3.53x             | **3.18x**         |   29.10 ms/MP    |   26.45 ms/MP    | 0.909     |
| p13    | 3.51x             | **3.11x**         |   28.97 ms/MP    |   26.21 ms/MP    | 0.905     |

Both campaigns: all cells byte-identical to C, same grid, same harness, same
box, neither side niced, no `target-cpu=native`. Two commits separate them:

* `29847e5d3` — the block-decision set was materialised FOUR times per frame
  (leaf `decision.clone()` alongside `decisions: vec![decision]`, aggregated
  up the tree, deep-cloned into a write-only `per_tile_decisions`, and the
  whole per-SB tree deep-cloned into its raster slot). Three of the four are
  gone. A/B: 1.072-1.111x at p10, 1.014-1.031x at p6
  (`alloc_decisioncopy_ab_2026-08-13.meta`).
* `6ad044d00` — `LeafEval::to_choice` cloned seven of the winner's buffers
  because it ran before `commit_leaf`; both callers now commit first and
  `into_choice` MOVES. A/B: 1.016-1.027x at p10, null at p6.

**p2 did not move and reads 0.7% WORSE, which is inside its own run-to-run
spread** (its 1024 cell is a single ~2.1 s encode and the fit leans on it).
p2 drives the encode through `depth_refine`, whose share of per-block time in
the decision buffers is far smaller than the fast tiers'; both changes are
per-coded-block costs, so the tier that spends 60x longer per block on the RD
search itself sees them least. Not a regression claim in either direction —
it is a null.

The port remains FASTER than C at 32x32 on every preset above 2 (0.46x at
p10/p13, 0.78x at p6) and at 64x64 on the fast tiers (0.81x), and its
per-frame intercept is still below C's at p10/p13 (0.87x / 0.97x). The whole
remaining gap is per-pixel slope.
